WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.175
Why this module?

2
00:00:01.175 --> 00:00:05.001
An administrator should sign in
with a phishing-resistant method,

3
00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:07.575
from a compliant device,
on a trusted network.

4
00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:11.525
And at the moment they activate a privileged
role, they should prove it again.

5
00:00:11.525 --> 00:00:14.466
That second proof is the activation gate:

6
00:00:14.466 --> 00:00:19.137
authentication context C one, and
its policy, PIM Activation C one.

7
00:00:19.137 --> 00:00:22.942
Microsoft Learn's PIM settings
page says PIM can require

8
00:00:22.942 --> 00:00:26.262
the context only after its
policy exists and is On.

9
00:00:26.262 --> 00:00:28.537
This is the first module that writes,

10
00:00:28.537 --> 00:00:31.799
so two guards stand between
the files and the tenant.

11
00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:34.889
Rule C A oh one fails any
policy file that isn't

12
00:00:34.889 --> 00:00:38.313
disabled and doesn't
exclude the emergency group.

13
00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:42.794
Every file carries the exclusion
whatever its state, because a file is

14
00:00:42.794 --> 00:00:47.199
enforced by changing one word; that's
this workbook's design guidance.

15
00:00:47.199 --> 00:00:51.199
And the apply refuses to start if
the pre-merge check has a finding,

16
00:00:51.199 --> 00:00:55.030
or if any policy it would write
leaves out the emergency group.
